          "annotations": [],
          "text": "{\"issues\":[{\"seed\":123,\"severity\":\"major\",\"layer\":\"simulation\",\"defect\":\"contradiction\",\"evidence\":\"Event 1 says, “Mina opened the wooden tube,” and the story repeats that she “opened the wooden tube,” but `tube.open` is `false` initially and finally and event 1 changes only `mina.knows.tube.label`.\",\"fix\":\"Either change `tube.open` to true in the read event (and add a later close event if needed), or revise the event and prose to say Mina read the outside label without opening the tube.\"},{\"seed\":123,\"severity\":\"major\",\"layer\":\"prose\",\"defect\":\"ungrounded_outcome\",\"evidence\":\"The response paragraph says, “The smooth kite settled beside Grandma,” while `kite.place` remains `roof` throughout the trace, including the final state; no event moves it to Grandma or returns it to the roof.\",\"fix\":\"Describe the tube/hello arriving without asserting that the kite settles beside Grandma, or add explicit movement and return changes for the kite.\"},{\"seed\":456,\"severity\":\"major\",\"layer\":\"simulation\",\"defect\":\"contradiction\",\"evidence\":\"The trace’s read event summarizes “Mina opened the wooden tube,” and the story says the same, but `tube.open` remains `false` from initial state through final state and is never changed by any event.\",\"fix\":\"Record the tube opening as a state change, or make the action a reading of an externally visible label.\"},{\"seed\":789,\"severity\":\"major\",\"layer\":\"simulation\",\"defect\":\"contradiction\",\"evidence\":\"Event 2 and its prose say Mina “opened the wooden tube,” but `tube.open` stays `false` in both the initial and final states, with no ordered change to it.\",\"fix\":\"Set `tube.open` to true when Mina opens it, or revise the event/story wording so that Mina only reads its label.\"},{\"seed\":789,\"severity\":\"major\",\"layer\":\"simulation\",\"defect\":\"wrong_knowledge\",\"evidence\":\"`tavi.knows.tube.label` is already `garden_birds` in the initial state. Nevertheless event 4 is titled `tavi_learns_truth` and summarized as “Tavi learned that the message belonged to the garden birds”; it makes no knowledge change, only `tavi.trust: false → true`. The prose likewise presents “When Tavi saw the words the garden birds” as the corrective revelation.\",\"fix\":\"Start Tavi without knowledge of the label and add a genuine informing/observing change, or frame event 4 as Tavi accepting or acting on information he already knew rather than learning it.\"},{\"seed\":789,\"severity\":\"minor\",\"layer\":\"prose\",\"defect\":\"unresolved_alternative\",\"evidence\":\"The test paragraph says the bell “rang a bright or low little song,” even though the trace fixes `bell.tone` as `low` throughout.\",\"fix\":\"Use the resolved value: for example, “rang a low little song.”\"},{\"seed\":789,\"severity\":\"major\",\"layer\":\"prose\",\"defect\":\"contradiction\",\"evidence\":\"Event 10 has already changed `tube.delivered_to` from `null` to `garden_birds`, but the ending says, “the message glided toward the garden birds,” which leaves the central delivery still in progress after it has been accomplished.\",\"fix\":\"Make the ending acknowledge the completed delivery, such as describing the birds receiving the message or responding as it arrives.\"}],\"strengths\":\"Seeds 123 and 456 have clear, ordered causal arcs: learning the recipient leads to a design choice, agreement, test, launch, and delivery. The prose generally realizes the stateful fin/tail, transfer, and flight-style changes vividly without exposing enum labels. Seed 789 also gives Tavi a meaningful role through the bell and tube transfers; its main weakness is that the intended realization turn is inconsistent with Tavi’s initial knowledge.\"}",
